# SubscriptionSavvy 2.0 — Full-Stack Implementation Plan

A complete personal subscription & recurring payments tracker. Serverless architecture, cross-platform (Next.js web + Expo mobile), with all 7 pages, 10+ features, and a stunning editorial UI.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Monorepo structure** — This will initialize a Turborepo monorepo inside `c:\Users\VARAD\Documents\GitHub\SubscriptionSavvy2.0`. The existing `.agent/` skill folder will be preserved. Everything else will be new.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Supabase account required** — You'll need a free Supabase project (supabase.com). After plan approval, you'll provide your Supabase URL + anon key and I'll wire them in. The schema SQL will be ready to paste into the Supabase SQL editor.

> [!WARNING]
> **Email reminders via Resend** — Requires a free Resend account (resend.com) and a verified sending domain/email. This will be implemented as a Supabase Edge Function (serverless, runs on Deno). If you don't have a domain, Resend allows sending from `onboarding@resend.dev` for testing.

> [!NOTE]
> **React Native / Expo mobile app** — The mobile app shares types, utilities, and Supabase client with the web app via the `packages/` shared layer. It will be built with Expo SDK 51, Expo Router v3, and NativeWind v4 for Tailwind-compatible styling.

